  "question": {
    "text": "Let $\\mathrm{A}=\\{-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3\\}$ and R be a relation on $A$ defined by $x R y$ if and only if $2 x-y \\in\\{0,1\\}$. Let $l$ be the number of elements in R. Let $m$ and $n$ be the minimum number of elements required to be added in R to make it reflexive and symmetric relations, respectively. Then $l+\\mathrm{m} \\mathrm{n}$ is equal to :-"
